# Decimal multiplication with integer operands

Multiplies 1.20 by 5 in both operand orders to verify the integer is
promoted and the result stays an exact decimal, producing 6.00 either way.

>>> source
integer_right: int = 5
decimal_left: decimal = 1.20

// Verifies the Decimal/Int promotion.
decimal_times_integer: decimal = decimal_left * integer_right
print(decimal_times_integer)

// Verifies the same promotion with the operand order reversed.
integer_times_decimal: decimal = integer_right * decimal_left
print(integer_times_decimal)

<<< stdout
6.00
6.00

<<< stderr
